    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> be the interior region between the lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> containing the origin. The set of all values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>, for which the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> lie in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>, is :",
